/-!
# The presentation of the second Conway group holds in its permutation model

The presentation selected for `Co₂` is Bray's presentation on the standard generators, an
involution `a` and an element `b` of order `5` whose product has order `28`, with ten relators
(`TauCeti.Sporadic.co2Presentation`). The generators `Co2.a` and `Co2.b` of the degree-2300 model
`TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2` both have order `23`, so they are not such a pair. This file gives two
permutations `Co2.imageA` and `Co2.imageB` of the `2300` points, of orders `2` and `5` with
product of order `28`, that satisfy all ten relators and generate exactly the model `Co2`, and
deduces that the presented group `SporadicName.Co2.Group` maps onto the model. In particular the
presented group is nontrivial.

Each image is given by its table of images, so that the relators compute directly. Both are also
written as words in the generators of the model (`Co2.imageA_eq`, `Co2.imageB_eq`), which puts
them in the model; conversely `Co2.a_eq` and `Co2.b_eq` write the two generators of the model as
words in the two images, so the images generate the whole model.

The two permutations were found by a computer search in the model: a random involution with `284`
fixed points and random conjugates of a fixed-point-free element of order `5` were tried until the
product had order `28`, and the four words come from a search in the Cayley graphs. Nothing about
that search is used: the relators and both directions of generation are checked here. Products
follow Mathlib's convention `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`, and it is in this convention that the relators
are evaluated.

No order of the model or of the presented group is asserted here, and the surjection is not shown
to be injective.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.imageA`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.imageB`: the images of the two generators,
  with `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.presentationImage` the resulting assignment.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.orderOf_imageA`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.orderOf_imageB`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.orderOf_imageA_mul_imageB`: the orders `2`, `5` and `28`.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: the ten relators hold.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.presentationHom`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Co2.range_presentationHom`: the
  homomorphism from the presented group and its range.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Co2`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, presentation `Co2G1-P1`, contributed by John Bray,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/pres/Co2G1-P1>.
* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Co2` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>, for the model in whose point numbering
  the images are given.
-/

